# Temporary local scratchpads
scratch/

# Claude Code local state. Sessions, worktrees and machine-specific settings
# stay out; the two things that are shared knowledge are negated back in.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git will not re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the trailing-slash form would make the
# negations below no-ops.
#
# launch.json is shared tooling and holds no secrets — it is the only file that
# tells an agent how to start this project's dev server.
#
# agents/ is tracked as of 2026-08-02. The definitions used to be generic
# downloads that a script re-fetched per machine, so leaving them untracked cost
# nothing. They are now hand-written against this repo's own gotchas, which
# makes them repo knowledge in the same sense AGENTS.md and .agent/wiki/ are —
# and an untracked roster means a clone, a second machine or a cloud agent gets
# none of it. `.claude/agents/**` (not `.claude/agents/`) so that any future
# subdirectory is re-included too.
#
# skills/ is tracked for the same reason, as of 2026-08-26. `/verify-gate`,
# `/review-change` and `/file-issue` encode §2, §3 and §6 of AGENTS.md as
# commands rather than prose — they are repo knowledge, and a skill that only
# exists on the machine that wrote it teaches nobody.
# rules/ is tracked for the same reason, as of 2026-09-03, and more sharply:
# a rule loads as an *instruction* when you edit its `paths:`, so one that
# exists only on the machine that wrote it does not merely teach nobody — it
# makes the same repo behave differently for two people.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/rules/**

# Agent-tool scratch directories. `.agent/skills/` and `.codex/` were deleted on
# 2026-09-04 (AGENTS.md §8); these entries stay so a re-run of any installer that
# recreates them cannot commit one machine's copies back into the repo.
.agent/skills/
.codex/
.gemini/

# i18n translation handoff packets. A working artifact, not a source: the
# catalog owns the English and src/locales/ owns the translations, and
# `npm run i18n:handoff:generate` reconstructs the packets from both.
#
# Untracked because Netlify's secret scanner matches short env values against
# the SHA-256 fingerprints these files carry — roughly one in 15,000 per hash,
# times ~120 hashes per file, times 15 files. That failed three deploy previews
# on 2026-07-21. Deleting them was the fix that kept undoing itself, because
# regenerating brought them back; now they are never committed in the first
# place.
# Untracked entirely as of 2026-07-22: task checklists are working notes for an
# active task, not product history. Files already committed remain in history;
# this only stops new ones. AGENTS.md reads this directory when it exists, so a
# fresh clone simply has no active task.
.agent/temp_instructions/

# Implementation plans, untracked as of 2026-09-06. They are scaffolding for a
# task in flight — approach, phase cuts, open questions — and they went stale the
# moment the task shipped: five folders, four of them for work merged weeks ago.
#
# ⚠️ This directory is therefore NOT the durable record, and the line above used
# to say it was. A plan never reaches a reviewer, a clone, another machine or a
# cloud agent, so a ruling that only lives here is lost. Anything worth keeping
# goes to the page that owns it (AGENTS.md §1): .agent/wiki/ for a design or
# workflow ruling, .claude/rules/ for something that binds while you write code,
# the issue or the PR body for the argument behind a change. Everything already
# committed stays in git history — `git log -- .agent/plans/` still has it.
.agent/plans/


# vitest 5 report and attachment output
.vitest/
